  "notes": "{沈|しず}む means to sink, go down, or feel depressed. Used for physical sinking and emotional states.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {沈|しず}む (intransitive): to sink\n- ⟦{沈|しず}める→沈める：02060_shizumeru⟧ (transitive): to sink something\n\nCONJUGATION (godan む-verb):\n- {沈|しず}まない (negative)\n- {沈|しず}みます (polite)\n- {沈|しず}んだ (past)\n- {沈|しず}んで (te-form)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{船|ふね}→船：00775_fune⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{沈|しず}む: the ship sinks\n- ⟦{太陽|たいよう}→太陽：03398_taiyou⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{沈|しず}む: the sun sets\n- ⟦{気持|きも}ち→気持ち：01385_kimochi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{沈|しず}む: to feel depressed\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{沈|しず}む: to feel down, be dejected\n- {沈|しず}んだ⟦{表情|ひょうじょう}→表情：03585_hyoujou⟧: a dejected expression\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- ⟦{沈没|ちんぼつ}→沈没：17516_chinbotsu⟧: sinking (of a ship)\n- ⟦{沈黙|ちんもく}→沈黙：13249_chinmoku⟧: silence\n- ⟦{沈殿|ちんでん}→沈殿：09136_chinden⟧: precipitation, sediment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{落|お}ち{込|こ}む→落ち込む：05750_ochikomu⟧: to get depressed (more colloquial)\n- ⟦{陥|おちい}る→陥る：14537_ochiiru⟧: to fall into (a state)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {沈|しず}んでいる: is sunk / is feeling down (resultative state)\n- Note: {沈|しず}む is a change-of-state verb. The ている form describes the resulting state — ⟦{船|ふね}→船：00775_fune⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{沈|しず}んでいる means \"the ship is sunk\" (on the ocean floor), not \"the ship is sinking.\" Similarly, ⟦{気持|きも}ち→気持ち：01385_kimochi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{沈|しず}んでいる means \"I feel down\" (a current emotional state). For the ongoing process, use {沈|しず}みかけている (\"is sinking\").",
